hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22860","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from al-Ala, from Abu Kathir, the freedman of Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Jahsh, who said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Jahsh informed me, who said: We were sitting in the courtyard of the mosque where funerals are placed, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sitting among us. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his sight toward the heaven, then looked, then lowered his sight and placed his hand on his forehead, then said: Glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah, what severity has come down. He said: So we were silent our day and our night, and we did not see it good, until morning. Muhammad said: So I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: What is the severity that came down? He said: Concerning debt. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if a man were killed in the path of Allah, then lived, then killed in the path of Allah, then lived, and upon him is a debt, he would not enter Paradise until he settles his debt."
"22861","Hushaym narrated to us: Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from al-Ala, from Abu Kathir, the freedman of Muhammad ibn Jahsh, from Muhammad ibn Jahsh, the in-law of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by Mamar in the courtyard of the mosque, sitting with knees drawn up, uncovered from the edge of his thigh, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Cover your thigh, O Mamar, for indeed the thigh is awrah."
"22862","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ismail narrated to us: al-Ala informed me, from Abu Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Jahsh, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by, and I was with him, by Mamar, with his two thighs uncovered, so he said: O Mamar, cover your two thighs, for indeed the two thighs are awrah."
